# Committed upstream signing keys, and what each one says about itself AS
# COMMITTED (issue #40).
#
# Every key here is the material behind a `# with key <fingerprint>` line in a
# recipe sidecar, exported minimal (`--export-options export-minimal`, so a key
# carries its own self-signatures and no third party's) from
# hkps://keyserver.ubuntu.com on 2026-08-28.
#
# WHY THE STATE IS RECORDED HERE. Expiry is a self-signature the holder can
# extend at any time, and extending it flips a past signature from EXPKEYSIG to
# GOODSIG with nothing about the signature or the bytes changing. Asking `gpg`
# today answers about today; this file answers about pin time, and
# tests/signing-keys.sh checks each row against the committed bytes so the two
# cannot drift apart.
#
# THIS IS NOT A TRUST ROOT. The fingerprints are corroborated by Arch and
# Buildroot pinning the same values, not by anything in this directory --
# committing the key makes the record stable and auditable, not
# self-authenticating.
#
